Looking at the rearranged figure, I can trace the dashed connection lines: piece A (the 1×4 bar), piece B (the 2×2 square), piece D (the L-shape), and piece E (the zigzag) each correspond to a section of the rearranged figure. The T-shaped piece C has no corresponding section in the rearranged figure — the fifth section of the rearranged figure matches the sixth (unlabeled) piece of the original rectangle.

Therefore, the piece missing from the rearrangement is C.

\boxed{C}
